1/28/2025 H COW:Passed
HB0131H2001/FAILED
Page 1-above line 1 In the catch title, delete "prohibition" and
insert "requirements".
Page 1-line 1 Delete "prohibiting" and insert "specifying
requirements for".
Page 1-line 11 Before "Upon" insert "(a)".
Page 1-line 13 Delete "hand".
Page 1-line 14 Delete "No" and insert "Each"; after "county clerk"
delete balance of line.
Page 2-line 1 Delete "official shall" and insert "may".
Page 2-line 2 After "ballots" delete balance of line.

Page 2-line 3 Delete line through "box." and insert "in accordance
with the requirements of this subsection. If a county
clerk establishes or uses a drop box in accordance with
this subsection, the county clerk shall provide notice
to the secretary of state of each drop box's location
not later than forty-two (42) days before any primary
and general election and shall ensure that ballots
deposited in the drop box are collected and returned to
the county clerk's office at least once during each
business day.".
Page 2-line 5 After "ballots" delete balance of line.
Page 2-lines 6 through 9 Delete entirely and insert:
". If a county clerk establishes or uses a drop box in accordance with this
section, the county clerk shall ensure the drop box:
(i) Is securely fastened to the ground or a concrete slab connected
to the ground;
(ii) Is secured by a lock that can only be opened by the clerk or
by a person designated by the clerk;
(iii) Complies with the federal Americans with Disabilities Act of
1990 and is accessible as determined by the county clerk;
(iv) Is under camera surveillance twenty-four (24) hours per day,
seven (7) days per week. The county clerk shall keep the recordings of the
camera surveillance for the same period of time that the county clerk is required
to keep the ballots in the clerk's possession.". YIN
